## Summary

Implemented **`DET.AMBIENT.Z_INDEX`** as a deterministic check aligned with the KS ambient plane contract (`forge-ambient.css`, `ks-animated-backgrounds.css`, `ks-living-background.css`).

### What changed

**1. `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-ambient-z-index.check.js`**

Replaced the stub with a real check that:

- Collects DOM evidence via `page.evaluate()` (live crawl) or accepts `metrics.ambientZIndexReport` (precomputed metrics).
- Targets KS ambient selectors: `.forge-ambient-bg`, `.ks-ambient-bg`, `.ks-section-bg.ks-ambient-bg`, `.ks-living-scene__global.ks-ambient-bg`, plus `.ks-living-scene` and ambient `canvas` elements.
- Flags four measurable violation kinds:
  - **`pointer-events`** — ambient plane accepts clicks (should be `none`)
  - **`z-index-high`** — ambient bg z-index > 1 (contract: bg 0, scrim 1, content 2)
  - **`stack-inversion`** — ambient z-index ≥ content wrapper z-index in the same container
  - **`canvas-layer`** — canvas inside ambient container with z-index > 1 or non-`none` pointer-events

Findings use standard fields: `severity`, `area`, `message`, `evidence`, `remediation`.

**2. `design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js`**

Registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS`:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| status | `implemented` |
| area | `first-screen` |
| scoreDimension | `visualRhythmFirstScreen` |
| priorityWeight | `8` |
| defaultSeverity | `warn` |

**3. `design-rules/registry.generated.json`**

Updated the `DET.AMBIENT.Z_INDEX` entry to match (status/area/score metadata). **Re-run `npm run blend-rules`** to refresh the registry fingerprint — shell was unavailable in this session.

**4. `auditor-tests/det-ambient-z-index.test.js`**

Unit tests for `parseZIndex`, `findingsFromAmbientZIndexReport`, and `run()` (metrics path + no-op when no evidence).

### Why

The source rule requires ambient canvases to sit **beneath** interactive layers per the CSS z-index contract. The check uses computed `z-index` and `pointer-events` — deterministic DOM/CSS signals, not AI heuristics.

